    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fly-half crisis",
          "heading": "Galthié admits fly-half shortage; Maxime Lucu in frame for Springboks test",
          "body": "Galthié says France are without their first, second, third and fourth-choice flyhalves for the Springboks test, with Romain Ntamack out for the rest of the competition and Antoine Hastoy, Matthieu Jalibert and Thomas Ramos all injured. Planet Rugby reckons scrumhalf Maxime Lucu, who came on at fly-half against Fiji, is in pole position to start in Paris. Galthié on him: \"We consider Maxime a scrumhalf who plays at No 10 for his club,\" while Axel Desperes, the youngster from Pau, is training with the squad."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa thrash Italy 66-7",
          "body": "England's Immanuel Feyi-Waboso limps off with leg injury."
        }
