    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Attacking edge",
          "heading": "Hugo Keenan's opener set Ireland's tone as both first visits yielded tries",
          "body": "The42's analysis of Friday's 42-12 win shows Ireland scoring with both first visits into the Argentina 22 and from both first set-piece platforms. The sharpest came in the 15th minute, when a right-hand lineout beyond the 10-metre line went to the backs: Craig Casey fed Sam Prendergast via Stuart McCloskey, and Hugo Keenan's first try followed. Ireland could not keep that edge in the final quarter, wasting a series of entries into Argentina's 22."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa thrash Italy 66-7",
