    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Turin defeat",
          "heading": "Muhamed Hasa sin-binned as Italy fold against Springboks in Turin",
          "body": "Saturday's Test at Turin's Allianz Stadium slipped away quickly: four Springboks tries came in a devastating 10-minute spell, and the visitors led 45-0 at half-time. Prop Muhamed Hasa's sin-binning made the second half harder still, as Italy's penalty count kept rising, and the match ended 66-7. The Azzurri arrived with a 16-strong list of unavailable players, including captain Michele Lamaro, and this was their fourth straight defeat."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England's Immanuel Feyi-Waboso limps off with leg injury",
          "body": "France's Hastoy, Jalibert and Ramos all injured ahead of Springboks."
