    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match verdict",
          "heading": "Planet Rugby: Rennie's All Blacks outclass Townsend's Scotland 43-21 at Murrayfield",
          "body": "Planet Rugby's winners and losers verdict says Dave Rennie's All Blacks have made themselves a serious force again, with the former Chiefs and Wallabies boss now on a 70% Test win record. For Scotland, the piece reads the second half as the problem: New Zealand kept a strong home side pointless after the break, and made their chances count. Beauden Barrett's two tries drew special praise, and the outlet says Townsend's men were left again on the wrong end of a familiar story."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa thrash Italy 66-7",
