    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Wing shines",
          "heading": "Louis Rees-Zammit ends eight-Test tryless run in Wales' Japan win",
          "body": "Louis Rees-Zammit was the standout as Wales beat Japan 28-21 on Saturday, collecting player-of-the-match honours after a flat, nervy game. He produced five of Wales' 16 line-breaks, made 121 metres and beat 13 defenders. Head coach Steve Tandy said: \"The best teams in the world have people that can break the game up, do something out of nothing.\" Wales now face New Zealand, the visitors in Cardiff."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa thrash Italy 66-7",
