      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ranking fallout",
          "heading": "Wallabies drop to 83.12 points after England rout, still seventh in rankings",
          "body": "Scotland, who sit sixth on 84.40, remain just ahead of the Wallabies after Sunday's Twickenham result. England's 45-22 win lifted them 1.31 to 86.99, leaving them 0.50 behind France in fifth. Australia shed 1.31 points to 83.12 and keep seventh place. Their three tries came from Max Jorgensen, Filipo Daugunu and Jeremy Williams, while England's seven included two from Henry Pollock."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
