      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fly-half crisis",
          "heading": "Eddie Jones starts uncapped Riku Kitahara at fly-half, without Ito on tour",
          "body": "Japan went into Saturday's Cardiff match without their first three choice fly-halves. Sam Greene and Seung-sin Lee are injured, and Ryunosuke Ito, who has started all of Japan's Tests in 2026, is back at university and misses the entire tour. Eddie Jones opted to start with Honda Heat's uncapped Riku Kitahara, with Toyota's Shinya Komura, who won the last of his three caps against Georgia in November 2025, the only other option on the bench."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa thrash Italy 66-7",
          "body": "England's Immanuel Feyi-Waboso limps off with leg injury. France's Hastoy, Jalibert and Ramos all injured ahead of Springboks."
        }
      ],
