    "467": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team reaction",
          "heading": "Morné van den Berg says Boks have plenty to fix before France",
          "body": "Morné van den Berg, who scored one of nine tries in Turin and was named Man of the Match, says the world champions still have plenty to study. \"There's a lot to improve on in our game, which is actually quite exciting,\" the 12-cap scrumhalf said. He conceded Italy put the Boks under pressure in the second half, adding that \"that's perhaps where we could have been better.\" The 66-7 win, he says, was vital for momentum before next week's Test against France at the Stade de France."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England's Immanuel Feyi-Waboso limps off with leg injury",
          "body": ""
        }
